// The data-provider stdlib is self-hosted. A datasource ships as a Tao declaration that states its
// configuration contract and binds behavior through the published provider protocol. A remote
// cache or sync engine uses this same shape with a different implementation fence.
// TR.DataProvider contract (conformance suite: TR.testProvider):
// - load(storageKey) returns one serialized starting snapshot or empty per schema mount
// - persist(storageKey, snapshot) receives each complete committed snapshot in order; a rejection
//   becomes schema error state and never silently drops the write
// - the schema owns loading | ready | error and notifications around those calls; the provider
//   owns storage only. Queries, identity, defaults, cascade, and reactivity remain runtime-owned
// - a provider implementation is stateless or instance-isolated, and must pass ordering, isolation,
//   empty-load, round-trip, and rejection conformance
// This full-snapshot boundary is deliberately narrow; incremental change/sync protocols remain a
// future provider family rather than leaking into the local persistence contract.
public
type Local is datasource with {
   StorageKey text

   provider LocalProvider from ./Providers.ts
}

public
type Memory is datasource with {
   // Memory has no configuration properties, so `Datasource Memory { }` instantiates it.
   provider MemoryProvider from ./Providers.ts
}

// Http is the query-driven remote datasource: entities stay ordinary `data` declarations, and the
// provider is offered each live query's descriptor (entity, equality filters, ordering, limit),
// fetches through the app's Adapter, and upserts rows by each entity's `(unique)` field. The store
// keeps evaluating every query locally over its rows, so a fill may land a superset. Fill lifecycle
// surfaces per query as `loading`, `refreshing`, `stale`, and `error`; `CacheFor` suppresses
// re-fills of a descriptor filled within the window. The Adapter declares the query shapes the API
// actually supports (`TR.Http.adapter` / `TR.Http.on`); a live query matching no declared shape
// fails loudly rather than silently fetching nothing.
public
type Http is datasource with {
   Adapter item
   CacheFor duration is 0.ms

   provider HttpProvider from ./Providers.ts
}
